-- title:
--   Perfect integral Serre pairing along prescribed boundary sections
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and write $R =$ [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), the subring of $\mathbf{Q}$ of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $c : X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be a morphism of schemes (universe $0$) that is proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, let $\varepsilon$ be a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} R \to X$ with $\varepsilon \cdot c = \mathrm{id}$, and let $\mathfrak{F}$ be a `FiniteMapData` for $(c,\varepsilon)$: affine opens $U, V$ of $X$ with $U \sqcup V = \top$, sections $f \in \Gamma(X,U)$, $g \in \Gamma(X,V)$ and an integer $m$, such that $U$ is exactly the complement of the image of $\varepsilon$, $U \cap V$ is the basic open locus of $f$ and also that of $g$, the restrictions of $f$ and $g$ to $U \cap V$ multiply to $1$, the $R$-algebra maps $R[T] \to \Gamma(X,U)$, $T \mapsto f$, and $R[T] \to \Gamma(X,V)$, $T \mapsto g$, are finite, and for every local $R$-algebra $S$ and every $s \in S$ the quotient $S \otimes_R \Gamma(X,U)$ by the ideal generated by $1 \otimes f - s \otimes 1$ is finite and free of rank $m$ over $S$. Let $\mathcal{V}$ be the associated two-affine open cover, with first chart $V$ and second chart $U$, and let $\mathcal{U} = \mathcal{V}.\mathrm{cover}\ c$ be the two-chart Čech datum with $A_0 = \Gamma(X,V)$, $A_1 = \Gamma(X,U)$, $A_{01} = \Gamma(X, V \cap U)$ and restriction $R$-algebra maps $\rho_0, \rho_1$. Let $\iota$ be a finite type and $\sigma : \iota \to (\operatorname{Spec} R \to X)$ a family with $\mathcal{V}$ sectional for $\sigma$: each $\sigma_i$ is a section of $c$, has image inside $V$, the images are pairwise disjoint, and the complement of $U$ is the union of the images. The assertion is that there is a family $\Lambda : \iota \to \mathcal{U}.\mathrm{LaurentChart}$, i.e. ring homomorphisms $\Lambda_i : \Gamma(X, V \cap U) \to R(\!(t)\!)$ carrying $\mathrm{algebraMap}\ r$ to the constant series $r$, together with proofs that (i) each $\Lambda_i$ is a completion along $\rho_0$ and the evaluation $R$-algebra map $e_i =$ `sectionAlgHom` of $\sigma_i$ from $\Gamma(X,V)$ to $R$, meaning that $\Lambda_i$ satisfies the predicate `IsRegular` for $\rho_0$, that for every $n$ and every power series $P$ over $R$ some $b \in \Gamma(X,V)$ has $\Lambda_i(\rho_0 b)$ agreeing with $P$ in all coefficients of degree $k < n$, and that for $b \in \Gamma(X,V)$ the coefficients of $\Lambda_i(\rho_0 b)$ in degrees $k < n$ all vanish precisely when $b \in (\ker e_i)^n$; (ii) each $\Lambda_i$ has a parameter for $\rho_0$, i.e. $\Lambda_i(\rho_0 b) = t$ for some $b \in \Gamma(X,V)$; and (iii) the residue sum of $\Lambda$ kills the range of the Čech differential on Kähler sections; and that for these data the integral Serre pairing $\mathcal{U}.\mathrm{serrePairingInt}\ \Lambda$, an $R$-bilinear map from $H^0$ of the Kähler sections and $H^1$ of the structure sheaf sections to $R$, is bijective as a map into $R$-linear forms on $H^1$, and so is its flip.
--
--   This is integral Serre duality for the two-chart Čech model of a smooth proper relative curve over $\mathbf{Z}_{(p)}$, in the form that produces the residue charts themselves: Laurent expansions completing the curve along the prescribed boundary sections, normalised so that the residue pairing between $H^0(\Omega^1)$ and $H^1(\mathcal{O})$ is perfect over the base ring. It is used in the construction of the integral lattice attached to the relative Jacobian of a modular curve model, where the duality identifies tangent-space data with $R$-valued functionals.
